/-!
# Non-vacuum, nonlinear control for the Ricci transformation law (ATLAS-II)

Old metric `h = −dt² + dr² + dθ² + sin²θ dφ²` (`Controls.Cylinder.gCyl 0`, first release; `R_θθ = 1`,
`R_φφ = sin²θ`, not vacuum). Coordinate change on `U = V = domEF = {R > 0, 0 < α < π}`:

  `Φ(T, R, α, β) = (T, R, α, β + λ sin α)`,  inverse `β ↦ β − λ sin α`,  `J = I + λ cos α E₃₂`.

`Φ` is not affine for `λ ≠ 0` (`∂_α J³_α = −λ sin α`, nonzero on `domEF` where `sin α > 0`; `λ = 0` is the identity), so the Christoffel transformation carries a genuine
second-derivative term. The pulled-back metric `gCtl λ = Jᵀ h(Φ) J` has the angular block
`[[1 + λ²c²s², λ c s²], [λ c s², s²]]` and the mixed Ricci component `R₂₃ = R₃₂ = λ c s²`, **nonzero exactly when `λ ≠ 0` and `cos α ≠ 0`**.

Two independent routes to the same 16 values `ctlR λ`:
* `ricci_direct`: the generated tables `Atlas/Controls/ShearTables.lean` (pd, Christoffel with the
  closed forms of `shear_spec.py`, pd Christoffel, Ricci), i.e. the registered `ricciOf` evaluated directly;
* `ricci_transport`: the general law `ricciOf_transform` applied to the first-release cylinder values.

Witness (`λ = 1`, `α = π/4`): `R₂₃ = √2/4 ≠ 0` (`mixed_witness`). Negative checks (wrong index placement,
missing Jacobian factor) live in `audit/atlas_ii/shear_negative.lean`, not here.
-/

open Real
open scoped ContDiff
open Matrix
open ExactVacuumAtlas ExactVacuumAtlas.Schwarzschild

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas.Controls.Shear

variable (lam : ℝ)

@[simp] theorem shear_0 (x : Pt 4) : shear lam x 0 = x 0 := rfl
@[simp] theorem shear_1 (x : Pt 4) : shear lam x 1 = x 1 := rfl
@[simp] theorem shear_2 (x : Pt 4) : shear lam x 2 = x 2 := rfl
@[simp] theorem shear_3 (x : Pt 4) : shear lam x 3 = x 3 + lam * sin (x 2) := rfl
@[simp] theorem shearInv_0 (y : Pt 4) : shearInv lam y 0 = y 0 := rfl
@[simp] theorem shearInv_1 (y : Pt 4) : shearInv lam y 1 = y 1 := rfl
@[simp] theorem shearInv_2 (y : Pt 4) : shearInv lam y 2 = y 2 := rfl
@[simp] theorem shearInv_3 (y : Pt 4) : shearInv lam y 3 = y 3 - lam * sin (y 2) := rfl

theorem shear_mem {x : Pt 4} (hx : x ∈ domEF) : shear lam x ∈ domEF := by
  simpa [domEF] using hx

theorem jac_mul_jacInv (x : Pt 4) : jacShear lam x * jacShearInv lam x = 1 := by
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [jacShear, jacShearInv, Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_four,
    Matrix.one_apply] <;> ring

theorem contDiffOn_shear : ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (shear lam) domEF := by
  rw [contDiffOn_pi]; intro i
  fin_cases i <;> simp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one, Fin.reduceFinMk, Fin.isValue, shear_0,
    shear_1, shear_2, shear_3] <;> fun_prop

theorem hasDerivAt_pd_shear {x : Pt 4} (hx : x ∈ domEF) (k i : Fin 4) :
    HasDerivAt (fun u => shear lam (Function.update x i u) k) (jacShear lam x k i) (x i) := by
  rw [← pd_shear lam x k i]
  exact hasDerivAt_pd isOpen_domEF ((contDiffOn_pi.mp (contDiffOn_shear lam)) k) hx i

end ExactVacuumAtlas.Controls.Shear

